# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Never commit a key. Bots scan public repos for tokens within minutes of a push.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# ── Model artifacts (derived) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ~1 MB, rebuilt in seconds by `python3 ml_engine.py`, and keyed on the data — so a stale
# artifact is worse than none. See DEPLOY.md §3.
artifacts/

# ── Fetched provider payloads (P2.2) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Raw responses are cached here so every published number can be traced back to the bytes that
# produced it. They are *not* committed: football-data.org's free tier is for non-commercial use
# and does not grant redistribution of its raw data. Derived datasets (data/*.csv) are ours.
data/raw/
data/staging/
data/provider_drop/

# ── Local scratch ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
_design/
.DS_Store

# Archives and screenshots dropped in the repository root while working. The leading slash matters:
# a bare `*.png` matches at every depth, which quietly excluded static/og/*.png, static/icons/*.png
# and static/apple-touch-icon.png — 65 files the site needs and the repository did not have. Every
# Vercel deploy is built from git, so those would have 404'd in production: no favicon, no PWA icons,
# no link previews on any page. The zip looked fine because it is made from the filesystem.
# tests/test_static_deploy.py now checks that every asset the page references is tracked.
/*.zip
/*.png

# ── Vercel ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The CLI writes .vercel/ when you link a checkout to a project. vercel.json is deliberately NOT
# ignored: it is the deployment configuration and belongs in the repository.
.vercel/
